\begin_layout Section*
Safety
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
El statement es:
 
\emph on

\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

nunca va a pasar nada malo
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset


\emph default
 (
\emph on
some bad thing does not happen during execution
\emph default
).
 Ejemplos:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
No es posible llegar a un estado de deadlock
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Se garantiza exclusión mutua
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
El sistema preserva un invariante dado momento
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We now formalize 
\emph on
safety,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Let 
\begin_inset Formula $S$
\end_inset

 be the set of program states,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\sw$
\end_inset

 the set of infinite sequences of program states and 
\begin_inset Formula $S^{*}$
\end_inset

 the set of finite sequences of program states.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We call elements of 
\begin_inset Formula $\sw$
\end_inset

 executions and elements of 
\begin_inset Formula $S^{*}$
\end_inset

 partial executions.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We will write 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma\vDash P$
\end_inset

 when the execution 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma$
\end_inset

 is in property 
\begin_inset Formula $P$
\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Finally,
 let 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma_{i}$
\end_inset

 denote the partial execution consisting of the first 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 states in 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For 
\begin_inset Formula $P$
\end_inset

 to be a safety property,
 if 
\begin_inset Formula $P$
\end_inset

 does not hold for an execution,
 then at some point some 
\emph on

\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

bad thing
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset


\emph default
 must happen.
 Such a 
\emph on

\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

bad thing
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset


\emph default
 must be irremediable because a safety property states that the
\emph on
 
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

bad thing
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 
\emph default
never happens during execution.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Thus,
 
\begin_inset Formula $P$
\end_inset

 is a safety property if and only if the following holds.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition*

\emph on
Safety
\emph default

\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\forall\sigma:\sigma\in S^{\omega}:\sigma\nvDash P\Longrightarrow(\exists i:i\ge0:(\forall\beta:\beta\in S^{\omega}:\sigma_{i}\beta\nvDash P))
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition*
Para demostrar que una propiedad no es de safety tenemos que dar una palabra que pertenece al complemento pero que no tiene prefijo malo.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Example*
La palabra 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $a^{\omega}$
\end_inset


\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 para la propiedad 
\begin_inset Formula $P=(a^{*}b^{\omega})$
\end_inset


\end_layout

