\begin_layout Section*
Liveness
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Informalmente estipula que 
\emph on
“siempre es posible que algo bueno ocurra”
\emph default
 (
\emph on
a good thing happens during execution
\emph default
).
 Ejemplos:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Un proceso dado termina su ejecución.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Es posible alcanzar un estado de estabilidad.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Si se llama al ascensor,
 este llegará en algún momento.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The thing to observe about a liveness property is that no partial execution is irremediable,
 since it always remains possible for the required 
\emph on

\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

good thing
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset


\emph default
 to occur in the future.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We take this to be the defining characteristic of liveness since if some partial execution were irremediable,
 then it would be a 
\emph on

\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

bad thing
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
 
\emph default
Therefore liveness properties cannot proscribe a 'bad thing',
 they can only prescribe a 
\emph on

\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

good thing
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset


\emph default
.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

We now formalize 
\emph on
liveness
\emph default
.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A partial execution 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha$
\end_inset

 is 
\emph on
live
\emph default
 for a property 
\begin_inset Formula $P$
\end_inset

 if and only if there is a sequence of states 
\begin_inset Formula $\beta$
\end_inset

 that 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha\beta\vDash P$
\end_inset

.
 A liveness property is one for which every partial execution is live.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Thus,
 
\begin_inset Formula $P$
\end_inset

 is a liveness property if and only if the following holds.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition*

\emph on
Liveness
\emph default

\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\forall\alpha:\alpha\in\st:(\exists\beta:\beta\in\sw:\alpha\beta\vDash P)
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition*
Para demostrar que una propiedad no es de liveness tenemos que dar un prefijo que no se pueda 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

salvar
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Example*
La palabra 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $aba$
\end_inset


\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

para la propiedad 
\begin_inset Formula $P=(a^{*}b^{\omega})$
\end_inset


\end_layout

